2. Evaluation license. If Licensor supplies the Materials without an executed
Order Form, Licensor grants the recipient a revocable, non-exclusive,
non-transferable right for 30 days to evaluate the Materials internally. The
recipient may run the company packages and inspect results, but may not train or
fine-tune a model, publish benchmark results, provide the Materials to another
party, use them in production, or create a competing task or environment set.

3. Commercial license. An executed Order Form grants only the rights stated in
that Order Form. Unless it expressly states otherwise, the license is
non-exclusive, non-transferable, limited to the named legal entity, and permits
internal evaluation and model post-training during the stated term. Affiliates,
contractors, hosted-model providers, and redistribution require express written
authorization.

4. Restrictions. Licensee must not: (a) publish, sublicense, sell, or expose the
Materials or substantially equivalent reconstructions; (b) make evaluator
references, private controls, canaries, or holdout variants available to an
evaluated agent; (c) remove notices or falsify provenance; (d) use the Materials
or resulting models for unlawful activity; (e) claim that fictional records
identify real people or operating companies; or (f) represent a disclosed copy
of the Materials as an uncontaminated holdout.

5. Derived artifacts. Model weights, aggregate metrics, and internal analyses
created through an authorized use belong to Licensee, subject to the Order Form.
They may not contain or enable extraction of substantial source files, expected
results, or other protected Materials. Raw or lightly transformed traces, task
